  "testHash": "30d02d1c2805a0d9b0ed5e5e2ff2d1eb0908e447b77a00a377ee8ecb763cf62a",
  "failsWhen": "The close refuses a row that a child completion legitimately changed (TASK_JOURNAL_MISMATCH), so the orchestrator must save the task a second time before it can accept it.",
  "trigger": "A producer creates a task, links a subagent, sends the subagent/end completion event, and the orchestrator closes the task with a result and evidence - with no task_update between the completion event and the close.",
  "oracle": "REQ-293 and AC-1 in the analysis record taskboard-write-integrity (business outcome: closing after a subagent finishes needs no task_update).",
  "realism": "The false refusal reported in the analysis: the row journal records create/update/close only, so a real delegated task whose child finished is refused at close until a redundant save. The orchestrator confirmed the realism of the criteria.",
  "realismReviewedBy": "orchestrator",
  "realismReviewedAt": "2026-11-28T11:04:53.000Z",
